#### Scala Issue

- **Bug**: When a class is declared with the comment after the class on the same line (and no `{` in the same line), the comment is highlighted as part of the class title rather than as a comment.
- **Root Cause**: In `src/languages/scala.js`, the class matching rule (the `CLASS` object) captures until it finds `[:={[\n;]`. If `//` comment is present right after the class header and before `{`, the rule incorrectly includes the comment in the class title highlighting because comment handling is not properly ordered or prioritized.

#### JavaScript Issue

- **Bug**: When comments appear inside parameter lists in JavaScript (within `(...)` of an arrow function or function), they are not highlighted.
- **Root Cause**: In `src/languages/javascript.js`, the `PARAMS` mode defines what can appear in JS function parameter lists. It tries to include `hljs.C_BLOCK_COMMENT_MODE` and `hljs.C_LINE_COMMENT_MODE`, but not in the fundamental mode that matches arrow functions with bracketed param lists. It appears some function parameter variants or placements do not correctly inherit comment highlighting, or comment modes are not always included properly for all param nesting cases.

